56
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:27,710
REVOLUTIONARY ARMY CHIEF OF STAFF SABO
ASSASSINATES KING COBRA OF ALABASTA

57
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:35,800
Dragon!

58
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:38,550
King Cobra's assassin...

59
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,390
wasn't me!

60
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,140
Yeah!

61
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:50,310
I believed you!

62
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:52,650
I did not need to hear it! I knew it!

63
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:53,860
But...

64
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,530
when I was at Mary Geoise...

65
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:01,450
I saw something unthinkable!

66
00:05:01,450 --> 00:05:03,280
Something unthinkable?

67
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,580
Kingdom of Lulusia
Grand Line

68
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:23,510
Hey.

69
00:05:25,850 --> 00:05:26,850
Look.

70
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,810
What is that?

71
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:34,560
It's creepy...

72
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:36,190
It's almost like...

73
00:05:36,190 --> 00:05:39,610
there's something massive up there...

74
00:05:41,450 --> 00:05:44,030
You cretins will all regret this!

75
00:05:44,030 --> 00:05:48,540
Once Marine Headquarters hears
about this, you'll all be impaled!

76
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:48,410
Princess Comane
Kingdom of Lulusia

77
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:48,410
King Seki
Kingdom of Lulusia

78
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:50,620
Dad, let me do it, too!

79
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,500
You vermin, I'll make you pay for this!

80
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,590
Your Maje– I mean, Seki, sir!

81
00:05:56,210 --> 00:06:01,970
If you had thought of your citizens
even a little bit, we wouldn't have revolted.

82
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:03,300
If I had what?!

83
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:06,970
Why should a king spare a thought
for his lowly citizens?!

84
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:10,060
Know your place! How dare you!

85
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:11,930
Please confess to your crimes!

86
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:14,190
We don't want to take your lives...

87
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:18,980
Just shut up and let me out of here!

88
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:37,880
In Pangaea Castle where
the Reverie took place...

89
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,340
on the Empty Throne...

90
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:43,550
Communications,
cut off your transponder snail.

91
00:06:43,550 --> 00:06:44,470
What?

92
00:06:44,930 --> 00:06:46,550
Did you not hear me?

93
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:49,060
Y-Yes, sir!

94
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:54,190
There's no king over the whole world,
so that throne should be empty...!

95
00:06:56,190 --> 00:06:57,650
Communications,

96
00:06:58,150 --> 00:06:59,610
listen carefully...

97
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:13,200
You did not trace any calls...

98
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:17,040
Dad, I'm scared.

99
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:24,340
You did not wiretap anything...

100
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,970
The Kingdom of Lulusia?

101
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:38,400
Such a country...

102
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:50,070
never even existed...

103
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,760
What's happening?!

104
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,580
Sabo?

105
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,080
Sabo?!

106
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,800
Seaquake off the southeast coast!
Prepare for a tsunami!

107
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:51,510
I repeat!

108
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:54,970
Seaquake off the southeast coast!
Prepare for a tsunami!

109
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:04,320
A Few Days Later

110
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:13,530
I'm gonna die! I'm dead!

111
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:22,540
It's cold!

112
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:24,130
I'm scared!

113
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:25,710
We're done for!

114
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:27,050
Help!

115
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,890
– A sea king!
– A sea king!

116
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,980
This is absurd!

117
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:52,570
Aren't you cold?!

118
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:54,780
It's all a matter of perception.

119
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:57,410
It must be good to be moss, huh?

120
00:09:57,410 --> 00:09:59,080
You're too dull to feel cold.

121
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,870
Want me to turn you into fish food?!

122
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:04,080
Try it!

123
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:07,340
Is this really the time?
Knock it off, you two!

124
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:08,300
Jinbe!

125
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:10,550
Watch out for ice floes!

126
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:11,760
You got it!

127
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:25,860
Furl the sails!

128
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:27,570
The winds are too strong!

129
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,070
All right!

130
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:39,290
Strong Right!

131
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:50,090
Move faster, Moss Head!

132
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:52,760
Can't you just work quietly?

133
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:58,510
Are we near the island yet, Nami?!

134
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:01,470
I don't think it's that far away!

135
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:06,020
I believe we've entered
the island's climate zone...

136
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:08,980
I'm guessing it's a harsh winter island!

137
00:11:14,950 --> 00:11:18,070
Seems like they're having
a hard time, so I'm gonna go help!

138
00:11:18,070 --> 00:11:19,450
Oh my,

139
00:11:19,450 --> 00:11:21,290
you look dashing, Chopper.

140
00:11:23,330 --> 00:11:29,250
Otama bestowed upon me this woven hat,
thus these winter storms pose no threat!

141
00:11:29,250 --> 00:11:30,090
Right?!

142
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:36,260
Hey, Nami!

143
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,640
What's that?!

144
00:11:38,090 --> 00:11:40,180
What's what?

145
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:50,940
What is that?!

146
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,690
That's a big warm eddy!

147
00:11:53,690 --> 00:11:55,530
An eddy?! That?!

148
00:11:55,530 --> 00:11:57,820
What in the hell is that thing?!

149
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,490
You've gotta be kidding!

150
00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:02,700
Why is it so far above the surface?!

151
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:07,000
It's a mass of heated water that's been
pushed above the surface somehow.

152
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
How hot would it have to be?!

153
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:13,250
It's like an afro!

154
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:15,460
Get us out of here, Jinbe!
We'll get pulled in!

155
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:17,090
Leave it to me!

156
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:18,090
Wait!

157
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,390
Someone's there! Inside the water!

158
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:25,520
What?! No way!

159
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,520
A mermaid?!

160
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:33,400
Somebody!

161
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,900
There's no mistake!

162
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,780
I hear a lady's scream!

163
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:39,150
From inside the water?!

164
00:12:42,370 --> 00:12:44,450
Are you serious?!

165
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,130
Even if someone is there, what can we do?!

166
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,210
We can just cut it...

167
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:02,890
If you so much as scratch the lady,

168
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:04,760
I'll fillet you!

169
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:06,100
Shut up!

170
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:19,360
One-Sword Style:

171
00:13:26,830 --> 00:13:28,700
Bird Dance!

172
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:37,130
– He cut it!
– He cut it!

173
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:41,970
Hey, guys!

174
00:13:41,970 --> 00:13:43,680
What's all the fuss about?!

175
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:45,220
Don't worry!

176
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:48,140
Woven-Hat Chopperemon is here, so–

177
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,310
The wind is so strong!

178
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:54,940
Why did you even come out here, Chopper?!

179
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,650
Help!

180
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,530
Chopper!

181
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,370
Luffy!

182
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:09,500
Not you too!

183
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:11,080
What are you doing?!

184
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:12,460
That idiot!

185
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:26,680
Jewelry Bonney "the Glutton"
Worst Generation

186
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:26,680
Bounty:    320 Million

187
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:28,890
A kid popped outta the water!

188
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,230
Who is that?

189
00:14:39,230 --> 00:14:40,150
Who are you?!

190
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,650
Thank good–

191
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,320
Wait, the monster!

192
00:14:46,570 --> 00:14:48,830
Oh, good! Seems like she's alive...

193
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:49,790
But...

194
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,870
Below you!

195
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:52,790
Where do they think they're going?!

196
00:14:50,870 --> 00:14:52,790
It's there!

197
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:56,250
That little kid's yelling something!

198
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:56,250
It's still there!

199
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:58,250
Below you!

200
00:14:58,250 --> 00:14:59,500
Look down!

201
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:02,130
"Look down"...?

202
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,970
What is it this time?!

203
00:15:11,970 --> 00:15:13,730
Go away!

204
00:15:13,730 --> 00:15:16,190
– Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh!
– What's going on?!

205
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:18,770
– Help!
– Help!

206
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:22,030
These waters aren't safe!

207
00:15:22,030 --> 00:15:23,070
Get us out of here!

208
00:15:38,210 --> 00:15:41,040
Is this it for us?!

209
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:43,880
Jinbe! Hurry up!

210
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:47,340
Jinbe! Get us out of here!

211
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:49,850
Hold on!

212
00:15:49,850 --> 00:15:52,310
Hurry!

213
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:02,610
What is that thing?!

214
00:16:02,610 --> 00:16:04,860
That's no ordinary shark!

215
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:07,860
It's way too big, and it's made of metal?!

216
00:16:10,370 --> 00:16:11,740
Hold on tight!

217
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,370
We're about to hit water!

218
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,210
Damn! They fell into the sea!

219
00:16:24,210 --> 00:16:25,880
This is bad!

220
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:27,170
Franky!

221
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:28,800
Take the helm!

222
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:32,470
Bring the ship around to us!

223
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,770
Alright! You can count on me!

224
00:16:45,530 --> 00:16:47,150
I told him to count on me,

225
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:50,110
but how do I find them
when the water's this rough?

226
00:16:50,110 --> 00:16:52,320
Guess I just gotta do it.

227
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,420
Ship's Bottom:

228
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,880
Rabbit...

229
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:14,430
Screw!

230
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:18,430
SHIP'S BOTTOM:

231
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:18,430
RABBIT SCREW

232
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,480
All right!

233
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,770
Time to mount a rescue!

234
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:40,750
Luffy! Chopper!

235
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:42,580
Where are you?!

236
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,470
Franky! Get us out of here!

237
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:53,930
Torpedoes!

238
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,600
Robin! Nami!

239
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:04,400
Oh, crap!

240
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:07,770
We're gonna capsize!

241
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:27,090
What was that explosion?

242
00:18:31,050 --> 00:18:33,180
Luffy! Chopper!

243
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:35,590
I'm here! You'll be alright!

244
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:46,560
Hey, you three! Stay with me!

245
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:48,020
We're about to surface!

246
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,530
The current is too strong!

247
00:18:56,530 --> 00:18:58,240
The rudder can't take it!

248
00:19:00,910 --> 00:19:02,950
Thank you, Jinbe...

249
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:05,750
I'm glad that all of you are okay!

250
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:11,420
The Sunny will be here soon!

251
00:19:27,310 --> 00:19:29,310
What's the matter, Jinbe?

252
00:19:30,570 --> 00:19:32,610
Hold on tight!

253
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,240
We'll escape below the surface!

254
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:40,280
Take a deep breath, guys!

255
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,130
Let's go!

256
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:11,270
Oh, no...

257
00:20:11,270 --> 00:20:12,860
The current is too strong!

258
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:14,230
We can't surface!

259
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,990
Somebody, help!

260
00:20:16,990 --> 00:20:20,240
Why am I underwater?! What's going on?!

261
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:22,700
Hang in there, Robin!

262
00:20:23,330 --> 00:20:24,830
Nami!

263
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:21,220
We're in trouble...
If we don't do something...

264
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,510
we'll all die.

265
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:41,740
Marine Branch G-14

266
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:41,740
At a Nearby Island

267
00:21:39,530 --> 00:21:41,740
All right, everyone!

268
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:45,200
Captain Tashigi
Marine Headquarters

269
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:44,240
It's time for your medicine!

270
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:47,330
One cup each!

271
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:48,410
You can do it!

272
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:53,830
I'll drink it, but only because
you told me to, Tashigi!

273
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,170
Thank you!

274
00:21:56,170 --> 00:21:59,380
Make sure you drink all of it!

275
00:21:58,710 --> 00:22:00,380
It tastes weird!

276
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:02,130
I don't wanna, it tastes awful!

277
00:22:02,470 --> 00:22:04,260
But you should still try!

278
00:22:05,930 --> 00:22:08,180
Do I have to drink the whole thing?

279
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:11,140
Yeah, to return to your original size.

280
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:14,270
I wanna return faster, so I'll drink two!

281
00:22:14,650 --> 00:22:15,730
Tashigi!

282
00:22:16,360 --> 00:22:18,440
I think I'm a lot smaller now!

283
00:22:19,570 --> 00:22:21,400
I can hardly recognize you, Mocha!

284
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:23,860
I can't wait to go home!

285
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:26,780
Yeah, be patient just a little longer.

286
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:27,870
Try to hang in there!

287
00:22:27,870 --> 00:22:29,450
Tashigi!

288
00:22:30,330 --> 00:22:31,750
Vice Admiral Doll!

289
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:33,960
Can I steal you for a sec?

290
00:22:37,250 --> 00:22:41,460
Vice Admiral Doll
Marine Branch G-14 Commander

291
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:41,460
Could you do something about
that Helmeppo brat?

292
00:22:41,970 --> 00:22:44,930
There's nothing I can do.

293
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:47,390
His best friend's safety is in question.

294
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:51,770
Captain Koby is an important
colleague to me, too...

295
00:22:51,770 --> 00:22:54,520
I'm begging you guys!

296
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:57,770
We're comrades, aren't we? Please!

297
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:04,700
Commander Hibari
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)

298
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:04,700
Lieutenant Commander Helmeppo
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)

299
00:22:58,650 --> 00:23:01,230
I'm beggin' you, too!

300
00:23:01,230 --> 00:23:04,700
Koby's always looked out for me!

301
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:07,950
Rear Admiral Prince Grus
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)

302
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:07,950
Please come with us to Pirate Island!

303
00:23:07,950 --> 00:23:09,370
Prince!

304
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,200
Please!

305
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:15,750
We can't do it on our own!

306
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:18,340
Prince!

307
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:20,170
I'm begging you!

308
00:23:20,710 --> 00:23:21,840
Please!

309
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:24,880
I won't move an inch until you join us!

310
00:23:25,510 --> 00:23:29,350
Koby's been taken to Pirate Island...

311
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:31,640
That's Emperor Blackbeard's home turf!

312
00:23:34,770 --> 00:23:36,270
You understand, right?!

313
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:40,270
If you poke that island even a little...

314
00:23:40,570 --> 00:23:44,490
bloodthirsty pirates will swarm you like bees!

315
00:23:47,610 --> 00:23:50,330
That's why it's called Beehive!

316
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:53,160
Egghead isn't far from here!

317
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:57,620
We could deploy the seraphim!

318
00:23:57,620 --> 00:23:59,380
The seraphim?!

319
00:23:59,380 --> 00:24:00,840
Are you out of your mind?!

320
00:24:01,630 --> 00:24:03,460
You need to calm down!

321
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:09,680
We can't even contact Drake right now...

322
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:12,100
There's nothing we can do!

323
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:18,230
You must understand.

324
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:23,020
Koby!

325
00:24:27,530 --> 00:24:29,280
What?!

326
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:31,490
Luffy's Group

327
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:31,490
Don't you know who I am?!

328
00:24:31,490 --> 00:24:33,330
Nope. I don't know.

329
00:24:33,740 --> 00:24:38,540
We were both labeled as part
of the Worst Generation!

330
00:24:38,540 --> 00:24:41,670
Oh, you're one of the worst, too?

331
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:44,130
This guy's an idiot!

332
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:50,300
I was there at Sabaody too, two years ago!

333
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:53,680
I'm Bonney!

334
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,600
Remember, we're enemies!

335
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:59,060
Then again, you did save me...

336
00:25:00,190 --> 00:25:01,480
So thanks for that.

337
00:25:02,110 --> 00:25:04,230
Don't mention it, Bogey!

338
00:25:04,650 --> 00:25:05,980
It's Bonney!

339
00:25:06,820 --> 00:25:08,070
What the...

340
00:25:11,110 --> 00:25:12,700
That's cold!

341
00:25:13,620 --> 00:25:16,080
I'm invincible with my woven hat!

342
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,160
I won't lose either, Chopper!

343
00:25:20,670 --> 00:25:22,250
This guy's an Emperor...?

344
00:25:22,710 --> 00:25:25,090
And Jinbe, Knight of the Sea,
really did join his crew...

345
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:28,550
Oh yeah, what's up with that wanted poster?

346
00:25:28,550 --> 00:25:31,510
Your hair was all white.

347
00:25:31,510 --> 00:25:33,470
It was all over the news.

348
00:25:33,470 --> 00:25:35,390
Oh, that's...

349
00:25:37,890 --> 00:25:40,270
just how I look when I'm free!

350
00:25:40,270 --> 00:25:42,190
What the hell?

351
00:25:42,190 --> 00:25:45,190
What happened to your crew?

352
00:25:46,570 --> 00:25:48,320
They'll be fine.

353
00:25:49,900 --> 00:25:53,490
What about your own ship and crew?

354
00:25:55,330 --> 00:25:57,080
I came here alone.

355
00:25:58,040 --> 00:26:01,540
That metal monster ate my ship.

356
00:26:01,540 --> 00:26:03,500
Screw that thing!

357
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:05,750
That's terrible...

358
00:26:06,130 --> 00:26:07,000
Yeah!

359
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,460
And I'm getting hungry now...

360
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:13,840
Oh yeah, me too!

361
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,850
Let's find a restaurant.

362
00:26:15,850 --> 00:26:17,350
I'm hungry, too!

363
00:26:17,350 --> 00:26:19,560
But, Luffy, do you have any money?

364
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,600
Hey, boneheads!

365
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,150
There's no restaurant here!

366
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:28,940
This place belongs to the government.

367
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:32,740
I'll fill you in.

368
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:36,700
This island is called Egghead!

369
00:26:37,200 --> 00:26:39,620
It's said to be 500 years in the future.

370
00:26:39,620 --> 00:26:42,710
It's the island that houses Dr. Vegapunk's lab!

371
00:26:44,210 --> 00:26:45,750
Vegapunk!

372
00:26:45,750 --> 00:26:47,170
I know that name!

373
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:52,260
I have business...

374
00:26:53,050 --> 00:26:54,880
with that quack!

375
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:12,280
Everyone! Are you all right?!

376
00:27:15,410 --> 00:27:18,620
Is the Sunny all right?

377
00:27:27,290 --> 00:27:29,540
A... A...

378
00:27:29,540 --> 00:27:32,590
– A giant robot!
– A giant robot!

379
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,550
Who could possibly...?

380
00:27:47,730 --> 00:27:49,310
Someone's coming out!

381
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:52,150
This won't do...

382
00:27:53,030 --> 00:27:54,940
Yet another failure.

383
00:27:57,030 --> 00:28:00,370
Why can't I suppress
the urges of living beings?!

384
00:28:02,290 --> 00:28:03,790
I'm at my wit's end!

385
00:28:03,790 --> 00:28:07,670
I don't know who you are, but thank you!

386
00:28:07,670 --> 00:28:09,000
You saved us!

387
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:13,250
The Mecha-Shark's only orders...

388
00:28:18,470 --> 00:28:21,680
were to scout, report, and bombard.

389
00:28:22,060 --> 00:28:25,350
But if it eats their ships,
there won't be any valuables left.

390
00:28:26,020 --> 00:28:28,350
It must be a programming error.

391
00:28:36,530 --> 00:28:37,650
Now...

392
00:28:37,650 --> 00:28:40,990
Who said anything about
rescuing you pirates?!

393
00:28:40,990 --> 00:28:45,660
I'm just a plain old genius scientist
working for the World Government!

394
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:52,000
I'm Dr. Vegapunk!

395
00:28:54,050 --> 00:28:57,800
– What?!
– What?!
